<title>USA: AMBAC qualifies eight muni issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>AMBAC qualifies eight muni issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMBAC Indemnity Corp said Wednesday it qualified for bond insurance the following eight municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--West Haven, Conn., $7 million general obligation bonds.  </p>
<p>--Windham, Conn., $21.945 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Urbandale Community School District, Iowa, $5 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Livingston County, Mich., $2.975 million water bonds.</p>
<p>--Poughkeepsie, N.Y., $6.425 million public improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Rome, N.Y., $6.662 million public improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Line Mountain School District, Pa., $4.995 million GOs, under AMBAC's direct purchase program.</p>
<p>--Montgomery Municipal Utility District No 40, Texas, $2.55 million unlimited tax bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
